{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Gad, a raiding band.</b> The raiding bands of Israel will gather after him, when they go out to the wars of Joshua, as it is said: ״חלוצים תעברו לפני אחיכם״ (you shall cross over armed before your brethren)." "<b>And he shall raid at the heel.</b> On his return from battle, he — his raiding band — will be at the rear (<b>עקב</b>) behind [the rest], after those who hate Israel. This is the way of warriors: when they go out to war they go first, and on the return they are last, to guard those returning from battle, lest the enemies pursue them. Another interpretation: <b>והוא יגד עקב</b> — he constantly pursues and is found at the heels of his enemies, like ״ידך בעורף אויביך״ (your hand on the neck of your enemies)."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:14.607023296Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}